# The first run of this rig reported "no #tool-field-cipher on this page; selects present: (none)"
# and produced an AES-128 file: the rig, not the site, was the suspect — the rail folds everything
# but its lead field behind "11 MORE OPTIONS", so the select was in the DOM and not on screen. The
# rig now opens the fold, refuses to run on a read-back it did not get, and the run below is the
# re-run with that fix (scripts/live-protect-proof.mjs).

